def rob(node):
    if node is None:
        return (0, 0)  # (robbed, not_robbed)
    left_robbed, left_not = rob(node.left)
    right_robbed, right_not = rob(node.right)

    robbed = node.val + left_not + right_not
    not_robbed = max(left_robbed, left_not) + max(right_robbed, right_not)
    return (robbed, not_robbed)

def house_robber_iii(root):
    return max(rob(root))
```

Every recursive call returns the full pair; the caller decides which half of each child's pair to use based on whether *it* is being robbed. The final answer, at the very top, takes the max of the root's own pair — the only place "pick the best of the two options" actually happens for the overall answer.
